// selfhost/parser/lib.sd
//
// v0.6 scaffolding for the self-hosted parser package.
//
// The runnable parser lives in `parser.sd` as a single consolidated
// module — the v0.6 `mty check` driver compiles one `.sd` file at a
// time, same single-file constraint as the v0.4 lexer. This file
// documents the intended v0.7 module layout once `mty-pkg` lands
// cross-file module resolution.
//
// ## v0.7 module layout
//
//   selfhost/parser/
//     lib.sd            // this file — package root + public re-exports
//     parser.sd         // cursor primitives + Parser type (the one
//                       // file we currently ship as `parser.sd`)
//     items.sd          // item dispatch (fn/struct/enum/use/mod/...)
//     types.sd          // type expression parsing
//     patterns.sd       // pattern parsing
//     exprs.sd          // Pratt expression parser
//     stmts.sd          // block + let + control-flow
//     agents.sd         // agent/protocol/supervisor (v0.7+)
//     concurrency.sd    // arena/task/budget/sandbox (v0.7+)
//     recovery.sd       // sync_to + error recovery primitives
//
// ## Public surface
//
// The exported entry point is `parse()`, which reads the trusted Rust
// lexer's token stream from the host bridge and emits CST events
// (enter / exit / token / error) via the same bridge.
//
// pub fn parse() -> Unit
//
// The bootstrap test in crates/mty-driver/tests/selfhost_parser.rs
// installs a SelfhostParserHost that:
//   1. seeds the token stream from the trusted Rust lexer
//   2. captures the event stream
//   3. rebuilds a CST tree from the events
//   4. diffs against the Rust parser's tree

package selfhost_parser_lib
